ation","items":[{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"It is indicated for  temporary relief of pain and pruritus from minor lip and skin irritations as well as for temporary relief from pain, burning, itching and discomfort associated with hemorrhoids and other anorectal/anogenital disorders.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB09345","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","items":[{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","text":"Drugs that block nerve conduction when applied locally to nerve tissue in appropriate concentrations. They act on any part of the nervous system and on every type of nerve fiber. In contact with a nerve trunk, these anesthetics can cause both sensory and motor paralysis in the innervated area. Their action is completely reversible. (From Gilman AG, et. al., Goodman and Gilman&apos;s The Pharmacological Basis of Therapeutics, 8th ed) Nearly all local anesthetics act by reducing the tendency of voltage-dependent sodium channels to activate.","source":"Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)","url":"https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/M0001169.html","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"}]},{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","items":[{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","text":"Pramocaine temporarily relieves pain, pruritis, burning and discomfort associated with minor lip and skin irritations and hemorrhoid's by inhibiting voltage gated sodium channels on neurons.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB09345","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Mechanism of Action","items":[{"section":"Mechanism of Action","text":"Pramocaine reversibly binds and inhibits voltage gated sodium channels on neurons decreasing sodium permeability into the cell. This stabilizes the membrane and prevents ionic fluctuations needed for depolarization stopping any action potential propagation.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB09345","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","items":[{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"There is minimal absorption after topical administration and it is not given orally.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB09345","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]}],"safety":[],"manufacturing":[],"structure":true,"populations":{},"reg":{"fda":0,"ema":0,"phase":4.0,"first_approval":1976,"bbw":false,"control":null,"withdrawn":[],"reg_checked":true,"aware":null},"chem":{"props":{"key":"cid:4886","title":"Pramocaine","products":4,"mw":293.4,"logp":2.97,"tpsa":30.9,"hbd":0,"hba":4,"rotb":9,"rings":2,"heavy":21,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C17H27NO3"},"similar":[{"key":"cid:123631","title":"Gefitinib","products":4,"mw":446.9,"logp":4.28,"tpsa":68.7,"hbd":1,"hba":7,"rotb":8,"rings":4,"heavy":31,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C22H24ClFN4O3","similarity":0.364},{"key":"cid:35949","title":"Morclofone","products":1,"mw":405.9,"logp":3.3,"tpsa":57.2,"hbd":0,"hba":6,"rotb":8,"rings":3,"heavy":28,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C21H24ClNO5","similarity":0.357},{"key":"cid:72385","title":"Nonoxynol-9","products":3,"mw":616.8,"logp":4.48,"tpsa":103.3,"hbd":1,"hba":10,"rotb":35,"rings":1,"heavy":43,"lipinski":1,"formula":"C33H60O10","similarity":0.34},{"key":"cid:3149","title":"Domiphen","products":1,"mw":334.6,"logp":6.06,"tpsa":9.2,"hbd":0,"hba":1,"rotb":15,"rings":1,"heavy":24,"lipinski":1,"formula":"C22H40NO+","similarity":0.333},{"key":"cid:3156","title":"Doxapram","products":2,"mw":378.5,"logp":3.17,"tpsa":32.8,"hbd":0,"hba":3,"rotb":6,"rings":4,"heavy":28,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C24H30N2O2","similarity":0.327},{"key":"cid:3091","title":"Dimorpholamine","products":1,"mw":398.5,"logp":2.1,"tpsa":65.6,"hbd":0,"hba":4,"rotb":9,"rings":2,"heavy":28,"lipinski":0,"formula":"C20H38N4O4","similarity":0.311},{"key":"cid:64949","title":"Pr